<p>Australia&#x27;s Royal Commission on Antisemitism and Social Cohesion released an interim report Thursday recommending tighter security at Jewish public events, firearms reforms and a review of joint counter-terrorism teams after the Dec. 14, 2025, Bondi Beach attack that killed 15 people during a Hanukkah celebration in Sydney. The report made 14 initial recommendations, five of them withheld publicly for national security reasons, and Prime Minister Anthony Albanese said the government would adopt all of them. The inquiry found Sydney&#x27;s Jewish community had warned New South Wales police of a high or likely threat before the Chanukah by the Sea event. The interim report said police appeared not to have completed a comprehensive risk assessment for the gathering. It also found Australia&#x27;s legal and regulatory frameworks did not hinder security agencies&#x27; efforts to prevent or respond to the attack, and The Guardian reported that the commission found no gap in current laws that could have prevented the shooting. Authorities have said the alleged attackers, father and son Sajid and Naveed Akram, were inspired by the Islamic State group. Sajid Akram was shot dead by police during the attack. The commission was established after December&#x27;s terror attack.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/08KJdpp2IX4Ai015jAcrudlT_9vaHX0_4BXob10c-nHXjpWP-MyjFwBJGPo8_ovzoFrY-WV0rxBhvQMbfDHWJvIWkXr2E7AV3ONsHvMtAg' alt='Grandparents of 10-year-old Matilda grieve at a floral memorial for victims of the Bondi Beach mass shooting in Sydney.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Threat climate: The report noted a sharp rise in antisemitic incidents in Australia since the Oct. 7, 2023, Hamas attack on Israel and said U.S. and Israeli attacks on Iran in February likely increased the risk to Australia&#x27;s Jewish community.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Prime Minister Anthony Albanese: Albanese said the report was consistent with the government&#x27;s plan for the inquiry&#x27;s first priority: examining the security elements of antisemitism and social cohesion issues. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330457654/australia-urged-to-tighten-security-after-bondi-beach-shooting'>Aaj TV</a>)</li><li>Sabina Kleitman: Kleitman, whose 87-year-old father, Alex Kleytman, was killed while shielding his wife, said agencies would need to do &quot;soul-searching&quot; over decision-making and restructuring. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/security-agencies-in-bondi-royal-commission-spotlight/'>Michael West Media</a>)</li><li>The Conversation analyst: The analysis said the interim report resembled an intelligence review and did not yet address deeper questions about conditions that may have fueled the attack. (<a href='https://theconversation.com/royal-commission-report-doesnt-help-us-start-making-sense-of-bondi-terror-attack-281859'>The Conversation</a>)</li><li>Community Security Group: The Jewish security organization urged police to provide armed officers for the Chanukah by the Sea event. The West reported that a senior police officer said no &quot;static resources&quot; were necessary. (<a href='https://thewest.com.au/news/nsw/jewish-group-warned-nsw-police-terrorist-attack-likely-a-week-before-bondi-beach-massacre-c-22214246'>The West Australian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/apr/30/bondi-beach-antisemitism-royal-commission-findings-ntwnfb'>Bondi royal commission: report calls for better policing of Jewish festivals after ‘high’ terror risk flagged for Hanukah event</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/inquiry-antisemitic-attack-left-15-dead-sydney-recommends-132522947'>Inquiry into antisemitic attack that left 15 dead in Sydney recommends gun reform</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/the-bondi-massacre-interim-report-is-out-dont-mention-the-g-word/'>The Bondi massacre interim report is